menu "Audio engine"

config AUDIO_SCRATCH_ENABLED
    bool "Enable vinyl/scratch mode (jog platter scratches the audio)"
    default n
    help
        When enabled, touching the FLX4 jog platter top while a deck plays
        scratches the audio (forward + reverse) by driving a read head over the
        per-deck PSRAM scratch capture buffer, instead of the Phase 1 platter
        hold+scrub. Releasing seeks normal forward playback to the head position.
        Additive: with this off the output path is unchanged and touching the
        platter does the Phase 1 hold/scrub. See docs/VINYL_SCRATCH_PLAN.md.

config AUDIO_DISPLAY_LATENCY_MS
    int "Output latency past the UAC ring, for the displayed position (ms)"
    range 0 200
    default 12
    help
        The engine position counts frames when they are mixed; they become
        audible only after the output chain. The UI shows the position that
        was mixed this long ago: the measured UAC ring fill (smoothed, read
        by the UI) plus this constant, which covers the isoc URBs in flight
        (3 x 4 ms) and the controller's own buffering. v260 HB logs: ring
        ~830-1280 frames at 48 kHz (17-27 ms), so ~35 ms in total.
        Raise it if the waveform still leads the audio, 0 = ring only.

endmenu
